				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Gt4Security Demo\n\n**Gt4Security** makes mobile vulnerability data *moldable*. It pulls from two free, real-time sources — **OSV.dev** (Android, Swift, Maven, PyPI) and **NVD** (iOS, device firmware, CPE-based) — and merges them into inspectable domain objects you can filter, drill into, and navigate without leaving the GT image.\n\nThis page is a live walkthrough. Every embedded example below fetches real data on first render. Click into any result to start exploring.\n\nKey classes: {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityQuery}}, {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerabilityGroup}}, {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerability}}, {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityAffectedEntry}}, {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityQueryResult}}.\n\nFor interactive exploration, see {{gtPage:Gt4Security — Playground|db=ay32zeq1d68a2o5v8gd9epf14}}."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-12T09:39:08.168853-04:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-14T22:51:45.64348-04:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "chjC114oQFOOBUbNd29Cdw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## 1. Cross-source mobile CVE overview\n\nOne query, two sources (NVD + OSV), deduped by id and alias, post-filtered by date. The result carries **provenance** — you can see how many came from each source, how many were deduplicated, and when the query ran.\n\nUse the **Summary** tab for the rollup, **Vulnerabilities** for the full sorted list, **By ecosystem** for the Android / (CPE-based) split (real OSV ecosystems — npm, PyPI, Maven, Android, … — plus a `(CPE-based)` bucket for NVD entries), **By CPE vendor** for the useful breakdown of CPE-based rows (apple / google / …), **Timeline** for the monthly histogram (click a month to drill into that month's CVEs), and the **refresh** button (↻) to re-run."
			},
			{
