				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## 2. Drilling into a single CVE\n\nClick any row in the Vulnerabilities view above, or inspect the result below directly. This is **CVE-2024-23222** — a well-known WebKit type-confusion bug exploited in the wild (base score 8.8 HIGH).\n\nTry these tabs:\n- **Summary** — id, severity, published/modified, malicious? flag\n- **Affected** — now returns `Gt4SecurityAffectedEntry` objects with parsed CPE (click a row to see vendor/product/version)\n- **References** — click any row to open the URL in your browser\n- **Aliases** — click an alias to look it up in OSV and spawn the related record\n- **🔗 toolbar button** — opens the first advisory URL in your browser"
			},
			{
