				},
				"string" : "## 3. Malicious package detection\n\nOSV mirrors the **OSSF Malicious Packages** database — reports of typosquats, credential stealers, and backdoored npm/PyPI/Maven packages. These show up inline alongside regular CVEs when you query a package name.\n\nGt4Security detects them via two independent signals: the `MAL-*` id prefix and the `database_specific.malicious-packages-origins` marker. Below is **MAL-2022-4301** — an npm typosquat of `libidn2`.\n\nCheck the **Malicious origins** tab for the reporter metadata, and the **Summary** tab for the `Malicious?: YES` flag."
			},
			{
